    <briefdescription>
<para>Internal state co-owned by <ref refid="classthemis_1_1storage_1_1_distributed_transaction_manager" kindref="compound">DistributedTransactionManager</ref> and all active <ref refid="classthemis_1_1storage_1_1_distributed_transaction" kindref="compound">DistributedTransaction</ref> handles via std::shared_ptr. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This ensures that a transaction can safely call rollback() in its destructor even if the owning <ref refid="classthemis_1_1storage_1_1_distributed_transaction_manager" kindref="compound">DistributedTransactionManager</ref> has already been destroyed.</para>
<para>Participants are stored as std::shared_ptr with a no-op deleter, so the caller retains ownership while still allowing safe reference-copying under the lock to prevent use-after-free when a concurrent unregisterShard() races with an in-flight prepare/commit/abort call. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
